& git show HEAD:common/Drawings/Format/Shape.js | sed -n 2952,3080p"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":7,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm rejecting PKT-0085. The cache can hand out stale text styles to a co-editor, which breaks the packet's `contract.preserve` rule that resolved text styles stay identical.\n\n**What checks out**\n- The code change is inside the target: only `external/sdkjs/common/Drawings/Format/Shape.js`, +80 lines. In the main repo only the packet file and `friction.jsonl` changed. The budget is respected.\n- `computeTextStyles` is the original body, unchanged. I compared the cache key with every input that body reads:\n  - the autofit values from bodyPr, or the temporary values while `bCheckAutoFitFlag` is set;\n  - the presentation `defaultTextStyle`, the master `txStyles` chosen by placeholder type, and the theme;\n  - the `lstStyle` of each shape in the placeholder chain;\n  - the shape's own `lstStyle` for that level, its fontRef and SmartArt fill.\n\n  Each input is either in the key or excluded from the cache. The document-editor language and PDF branches can't be reached because of the presentation-only, non-PDF guard.\n- The Executor log is filled in, and there is no `.theseus/spawn/` directory.\n\n**Blocking problem**\n- The key holds only object Ids, not their content, so the cache is only correct if layouts, masters and placeholder shapes cannot change while it is on. The only thing that turns it off is a local history point (`History.Index !== -1` or `Points.length > 0`).\n- Changes from co-editors are applied without creating a local history point. Take a user who opens a deck and only views it, or hasn't edited yet: their History stays empty. If a co-editor changes a layout or master placeholder's `lstStyle`, or the master `txStyles`, a later recalculation finds the old entry under the same key and shows outdated fonts, sizes and spacing.\n- The executor names this risk but did nothing about it. There is no guard and no follow-up packet in `.theseus/spawn/` or the \"Spawned packets\" section, even though the log calls the version counter a \"follow-up candidate\".\n\n**Smaller gaps**\n- No benchmark was run on deck-50.pptx, so whether the refactor is worth it is unproven.\n- No test covers a cache hit next to a miss, or the switch-off on the first history point. The oracle only shows that nothing else regressed.\n\n**What would fix it, all inside Shape.js**\n- Turn the cache off (and clear it) whenever co-editing is active or remote changes have been applied. For example, check the collaborative-editing state or `isCoAuthoringEnable`, or limit the cache to the document-open phase.\n- Alternatively, if a version counter is chosen instead, record it as a follow-up request in `.theseus/spawn/`.\n- Ideally, also add a test that a hit returns the same styles as a miss.\n\nI didn't change any files.\n\nVERDICT: REJECT cache key uses only Ids and the only switch-off is a local history point, so a co-editor with an empty History gets stale styles after a remote change (breaks contract.preserve); turn the cache off when co-editing is active or remote changes arrive, or file the version-counter follow-up in .theseus/spawn/","ttft_ms":4049,"type":"result","duration_ms":44729,"uuid":"c29982f7-af71-479e-a4d6-03279ef8c114","ttft_stream_ms":2364,"time_to_request_ms":393,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":248,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":20,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":5,"transcript_persist":23,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_m